.TH UITODO 1
.SH NAME
uitodo, uicount \- programs on ui(4)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uitodo
[
.B -f
.I file
]
.PP
.B uicount
.SH DESCRIPTION
Both run in a new window of
.IR ui (4),
written in Rust with
.IR uiview (2).
.PP
.I Uitodo
keeps a list of things to do.
A text box takes a new one (enter, or the
.B add
button); each has a check box (done) and a button that takes it away.
With
.BR -f ,
the list is read from
.I file
at the start and written to it after each change, a line each:
.B 0
or
.B 1
(done), a blank, the text.
.PP
.I Uicount
counts: a number and buttons to add one, take one, and start again.
.PP
The windows' files are those of
.IR ui (4):
.B /srv/ui.\fIuser\fP.\fIpid\fP.0
mounted elsewhere shows the list's tree and changes it.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/uidemo
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ui (4),
.IR uiview (2)
